# Project

Everything the agents and skills need about *your* project, they read from here.

The fastest way to fill this in is the **`onboard`** skill — it asks a few questions
and writes this file for you. You can also edit it by hand: replace the placeholders
below. This is the one file that's truly project-specific.

## App
- **Base URL (local):** `http://localhost:3000`
- **Base URL (staging):** `https://staging.example.com`
- **Base URL (prod):** *(optional — usually you don't run E2E against prod)*
- **Auth for tests:** <how a test logs in — a seeded test user, a saved
  `storageState`, or env vars. The seed shows UI login; prefer a fixture in practice.>

> `baseURL` must also be set in `playwright.config` so relative `page.goto('/path')`
> calls (like the seed's) resolve. `onboard` sets this up for new projects.

## Test command
- **Run all:** `npx playwright test`
- **Run one file:** `npx playwright test tests/<feature>.spec.ts`
- **Run one browser:** `npx playwright test --project=chromium`
- **Run a tag:** `npx playwright test --grep @smoke`
- **Headed / UI mode:** `npx playwright test --ui`
- **Open a failure trace:** `npx playwright show-trace`
- **Record a flow / find locators:** `npx playwright codegen <url>`

## Where things live
- **Plans (human-readable):** `specs/`
- **Tests:** `tests/`
- **Fixtures / page objects:** `tests/fixtures/`, `tests/pages/`

## Tickets
- **Source:** <pick one — `paste` (no integration), or a tracker: Jira `PROJ`,
  Linear, GitHub Issues, etc.>
- **Tracker base URL:** `https://your-org.atlassian.net` *(only if wiring a tracker MCP)*

> A tracker is optional. With `paste`, drop the acceptance criteria into the prompt and
> `plan-tests` works the same way. To wire one, see `.env.example` and `.mcp.json`.
